SUMMARY:2026 Jersey City Art and Studio Tour (JCAST)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Side JC presents the 2026 Jersey City Art & Studio Tour (JCAST)\, the 37th edition from October 1st to the 4th\, with the theme\, Unbounded Nature. JCAST is a robust city-wide series featuring 150+ arts venues (in the 6 wards) presenting visual art including 200+ artist studios with 5 signature exhibitions to showcase both the best\, diverse\, and inclusive works of Jersey City artists\, not just limited to fine art and with performance\, music\, poetry\, and film. \nIt begins with a Kick-Off Opening event featuring the Jersey City Legend Awards and features 100+ art gallery and art exhibitions\, 50+ poetry\, music and film events\, 25+ art workshops for kids and adults\, 10+ art\, murals\, bus and walking tours\, throughout the city\, and concludes with a closing party. \nJCAST is sponsored by the City of Jersey City\, Office of Cultural Affairs\, Educational Arts Team\, 902 Brewing Company\, Jersey City Arts Council\, JCEDC\, Jersey City Arts + Culture Trust Fund and partners with the Jersey City Free Public Library\, Liberty State Park\, Saint Peter’s University\, The Bethune Center\, Central Avenue Special Improvement District (SID)\, Historic Downtown Jersey City Special Improvement District (SID)\, Jersey City Book Fair\, NJ TRANSIT\, and has WBGO\, WFMU and WMSC of Montclair State University as radio station media partners\, coLAB Arts as a fiscal sponsor and The Creative Side JC as the producer. Find details and register to attend at www.jerseycityarts.org and contact@jerserycityarts.org \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/2026-jersey-city-art-and-studio-tour-jcast/
LOCATION:NJ
CATEGORIES:Art & Culture,Entertainment,Kids & Families
