SUMMARY:UUCM Religious Education Registration
DESCRIPTION:Registration is now open for the Unitarian Universalist Congregation at Montclair’s 2026-2027 Religious Education (RE) program for children and youth. We are a liberal religious community seeking transformation in our hearts\, our homes\, our community\, and our world. \nReligious Education (RE) Program Goals: The RE program aims to provide broad and connected Unitarian Universalist lifespan religious education for the community inside and outside our walls to ensure a vibrant\, thriving congregation. \nThe purpose of the Religious Education Program is to guide our children\, youth\, and adults in the ethical exploration of Unitarian Universalist Values. We help to nurture the curiosity of soul expansion and growth through fun and engaging structured learning and spiritual experiences that emphasize: \nNurturing the individual spirit within our loving community.\nUnderstanding that we are part of the Unitarian Universalist heritage\, past\, present\, and future.\nCultivating curiosity about\, appreciation for\, and engagement with all faith traditions.\nDeveloping a lifelong practice of service.\nEncouraging mindfulness and a sense of wonder. \nPROGRAM INFO:\nUnitarian Universalists are a covenantal\, like-valued people. The covenants we make are intentional conversations about the value-based actions we expect from each other\, and they hold us accountable and in community by giving everyone a voice. The Living Tradition of Unitarian Universalism is informed by growth and change. UUCM affirms and promotes the UU Values that call us to do something about what we believe ethically and responsibly. These UU Values are: \nJustice\nEquity\nTransformation\nPluralism\nInterdependence\nGenerosity\nThese UU Values are all held together with the common thread of LOVE. \nOur RE Program provides a liberating faith education that instills values that emancipate minds and grow spirits. Our dogma-free approach centers the margins\, widens the circle\, and enlivens the human impulse to justice and love. \nClasses on Offer for 2026-2027:\n4th/5th Grade OWL Class (4-5 in the Spring)\n8th/9th Grade OWL – 8th & 9th grades\nLiving Into Social Justice – Trimester 1 of 8th/9th OWL\nCreative Edge – 3rd to 5th grades\nDungeons & Dragons – 4th through 12th grades The D&D CLASS SIZE LIMIT is 8 students.\nNeighboring Faiths – 6th & 7th grades\nValues Room – K through 3rd grades (4-year-old Pre-K are allowed w/parent assisting\, 5-year-olds are independent)\nYouth Group (U-YG) – 9th through 12th grades \nHIKE! Two Special COMMUNITY-BUILDING Hiking Events\, one in the Fall and one in the Spring: \nRE Friends & Families HIKES – Outdoor Education engages participants in practical and active learning experiences\, typically in natural settings\, to benefit the person\, community\, and nature. \nDetailed DESCRIPTIONS of our 2026-2027 Classes & Activity Groups offerings: \nOWL- 8th & 9th grade OWL (Oct 26 to May 27)\, and 4th & 5th grade OWL will take place in the Spring of 2027 – Our Whole Lives (OWL)\nOWL is a comprehensive\, lifespan sexuality education curriculum for use in both secular settings and faith communities. It dismantles stereotypes and assumptions\, builds self-acceptance and self-esteem\, fosters healthy relationships\, improves decision-making\, and has the potential to save lives. \nLIVING INTO SOCIAL JUSTICE – (ONLY for Trimester 1 pre-8th/9th grade OWL – formerly called Heeding The Call).\nA social justice curriculum exploring ethical imagination and moral courage by examining societal oppression while encouraging an understanding of values that counteract the marginalization of others. Workshops on empathy\, courage\, abundance\, joy\, and other values ask participants to recognize how these standards can be tools for Justice. Additionally\, the program includes concrete tools\, such as suggestions on how to be a good ally and tips on the language of conflict resolution. \nCREATIVE EDGE – Best 3rd through 5th Grades. Multifaceted creative exploration of foundational UU values.\nStudents will learn how to frame our UU Values and concepts like dignity\, justice\, and compassion and to capture and convey powerful messages through creative projects using various media – Poetry\, Spoken Word\, Music\, Painting\, drawing\, photography\, fabric arts\, etc. Creative Edge also engages with the wider UUCM congregation by inviting our creative congregants to share their special creative talents with the kids. Our multi-age learning environment encourages multi-age peer support and mentoring. \nTHE VALUES ROOM – Best for Kindergarten through 3RD Grades and New to the U kids. Multifaceted creative exploration of foundational UU values.\nStudents will learn how to frame concepts like dignity\, justice\, and compassion and to capture and convey powerful messages through creative projects using various media. Our multi-age learning environment encourages multi-age peer support and mentoring. \nDUNGEONS & DRAGONS – For 4th through 12th grades. Explores CORE UU VALUES and TRADITIONS through D&D fantasy role-playing adventures.\nA creative role-playing game where students create characters that offer kids who are already grappling with complicated questions about their lives ways to safely explore different aspects of themselves and society. Drop-Ins are limited (available only with advanced notice/Teacher permission). \nNEIGHBORING FAITHS (6th & 7th Grades)\nIn the Neighboring Faith class\, young people become better citizens by learning about other faith communities\, through field trips to those faith communities. We focus on three important dimensions of religion; the emotional\, the material\, and the social. We learn about these dimensions of religion by experiencing the worship services of other faith communities. \nUU YOUTH GROUP (U-YG)\nService opportunities and Youth bonding experiences through regular meetings and interactions within the ministry areas of UUCM. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/uucm-religious-education-registration/
LOCATION:UU Congregation at Montclair\, 67 Church Street\, Montclair\, NJ\, United States
CATEGORIES:Kids & Families
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/RE-26-27.png
ORGANIZER;CN="UU Congregation at Montclair":MAILTO:OFFICEMGR@UUMONTCLAIR.ORG
END:VEVENT
